1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
You've woken up with Megumi's Ten Shadows, from

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,860
Jujutsu Kaisen.

3
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:05,300
In real life.

4
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:07,700
Your shadow is alive.

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,340
And it's hungry.

6
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,440
One of the things inside it will help

7
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,200
you save a car park full of people.

8
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:16,820
Another has never been tamed by anyone but

9
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,440
Sukuna, and in forty days you'll be tempted

10
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,260
to open it.

11
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,640
But right now it's three fifteen in the

12
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:22,820
morning,

13
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,740
the moon is on your floor, and your

14
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,400
shadow has just stopped copying you.

15
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,580
You lift your arm.

16
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:32,940
The shadow on the floor doesn't.

17
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:35,680
Then two dogs step out of it, one

18
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,180
white and one black, and sit in front

19
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:39,920
of you like they've been waiting all night.

20
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,540
In the story these are the Divine Dogs,

21
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,280
the first shikigami every user of the Ten

22
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,380
Shadows Technique receives.

23
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:47,920
They hunt curses.

24
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,980
Your cat, who respects nothing, leaves the room.

25
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,540
Then they catch a scent and drag you

26
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,740
out of the flat, down the stairs, across

27
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:57,560
the empty city.

28
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,890
A dog can have up to about three

29
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:03,420
hundred million scent receptors, against about six million

30
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:04,060
in a human.

31
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:06,640
That's the best case, but it explains why

32
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,560
they're not slowing down.

33
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:09,220
They stop under a rooftop.

34
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:13,120
On it, there's your neighbour's lost cat.

35
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:13,880
It looks at you.

36
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:15,720
It's not impressed either.

37
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,040
Lesson one:

38
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,040
your shadow has a perfect nose, and no

39
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:20,860
idea what's yours.

40
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,320
At breakfast you try to act normal.

41
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,940
Your mum asks why you're sitting so far

42
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:27,600
from the table.

43
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:29,480
The dogs are under it.

44
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:31,180
You can feel them breathing.

45
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,540
Every time she moves, they move with her

46
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:34,920
shadow,

47
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:36,800
and you realise something:

48
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,840
they're not following her.

49
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,620
They're guarding you.

50
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,000
You eat a whole bowl of cereal with

51
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,440
your feet pulled up on the chair.

52
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:45,900
Lesson two:

53
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:47,680
they obey you.

54
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,560
But they don't understand "normal".

55
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:52,960
At lunch you try the next one, as

56
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,100
quietly as you can.

57
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,300
Something wet slaps out of your shadow and

58
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,320
onto the office floor:

59
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,600
a toad the size of a person.

60
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:04,540
In the story this is Toad, another shikigami.

61
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,840
And in the story, two of them can

62
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,100
even fuse into something new.

63
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,020
You hide it in the kitchen fridge.

64
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,620
It leaves a tongue's worth of mess on

65
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:13,000
the printer.

66
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:16,240
Your boss asks who's been feeding the printer.

67
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:18,020
Lesson three:

68
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:21,280
these things don't come with a manual, and

69
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:23,080
they don't ask permission to appear.

70
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,500
In the evening you take it all to

71
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:29,660
an empty underground car park, because you want

72
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:30,780
to know where your limit is.

73
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,160
In the story,

74
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:35,340
Max Elephant takes a huge amount of cursed

75
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:36,200
energy to summon.

76
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:40,580
An adult African elephant weighs about six tonnes.

77
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:43,680
Our own maths: drop six thousand kilograms from

78
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,360
three metres, and you get roughly one hundred

79
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,760
and seventy-six thousand joules.

80
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,060
You summon it.

81
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,460
You make it stand up.

82
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,940
Then your legs go, and you sit on

83
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:57,260
the concrete, shaking, because it took everything you

84
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,660
had just to hold it there.

85
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,500
You spend an hour finding where you left

86
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:01,940
your keys.

87
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:03,720
Lesson four:

88
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,180
the bigger the shadow,

89
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:06,460
the bigger the bill,

90
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,040
and you're the one who pays.

91
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:11,860
On day three, you try the Great Serpent,

92
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,160
a big white snake with black marks across

93
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:15,680
its body.

94
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,760
The longest wild snake ever measured is a

95
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,600
reticulated python of seven point two two metres,

96
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:25,220
confirmed by Guinness in twenty twenty-six.

97
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,440
Yours fills the hallway.

98
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,300
You can't tell where it ends.

99
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:31,480
Your neighbour opens her door, looks at the

100
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,800
white coil blocking the stairs, and goes back

101
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,820
inside without a word.

102
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:37,820
She never mentions it again, even when you

103
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:38,640
meet in the lift.

104
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,300
Lesson five:

105
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,180
when something is bigger than your building, you

106
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:44,460
have to learn to put it back.

107
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:49,000
In the story, two shikigami can fuse into

108
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:49,760
something new.

109
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,920
So, of course, you try it.

110
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:53,620
You call two at once.

111
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:55,420
They don't merge.

112
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:56,780
They tangle.

113
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,660
For ten seconds there's a creature in your

114
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:01,760
stairwell that has too many legs and the

115
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,680
wrong number of opinions about it.

116
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,000
You manage to send them back, but it

117
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,200
takes everything you have.

118
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,860
You spend the next day in bed.

119
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:12,500
Lesson six: more is not stronger.

120
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,320
More is just more.

121
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,800
A boy in the park films your shadow

122
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,380
at sunset.

123
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,320
It's the wrong shape.

124
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,720
It has ears, and it's wagging.

125
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,720
The video spreads.

126
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,640
Half the comments say it's CGI.

127
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:29,820
The other half say it's a ghost dog.

128
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:32,720
Nobody says "shikigami", because only a few people

129
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,640
know what that means, and they think it's

130
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,000
a joke.

131
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:39,080
Lesson seven: the people who'd understand are the

132
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,800
ones who'd never believe it.

133
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,700
On day twelve you take it to an

134
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,300
empty football pitch, at night, to try something

135
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:46,700
bigger.

136
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,800
In the story, Megumi's version of a Domain

137
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:52,160
Expansion is called Chimera Shadow Garden.

138
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,820
It has no walls, no closed barrier.

139
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,800
It spreads his shadow over whatever is already

140
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,200
there.

141
00:04:58,880 --> 00:04:59,620
And it's incomplete.

142
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:02,660
So you push your shadow outwards, across the

143
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,780
grass, until the whole pitch is dark under

144
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:05,200
your feet.

145
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,800
The dogs run through it faster than anything

146
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,080
you've ever seen, as if the ground itself

147
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:10,980
was helping them.

148
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,620
But nothing hits for you.

149
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:14,720
Nothing wins for you.

150
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:17,080
It's only a place where everything you call

151
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:17,920
comes out easier.

152
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,420
You hold it for a minute, and your

153
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,300
head feels like it's full of wet sand.

154
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,400
Lesson eight: the garden doesn't fight.

155
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,340
It just makes the fight yours.

156
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:30,940
A man in a grey suit sits down

157
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:33,100
at your table in a café and doesn't

158
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,600
ask a single question.

159
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,520
He slides a card across.

160
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,240
He's not interested in what you can do.

161
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:42,040
He wants to know what you'd refuse to

162
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:42,340
do.

163
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,840
You say you don't know yet.

164
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,860
He nods, as if that was the right

165
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:49,200
answer, and leaves without his coffee.

166
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,440
Lesson nine:

167
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:54,200
the first question anyone asks about power is

168
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,940
how far you'd go.

169
00:05:56,960 --> 00:06:00,820
On day twenty something stirs in your shadow

170
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:04,000
that isn't a dog, or a toad, or

171
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:04,540
an elephant.

172
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:09,000
In the story, it's called Mahoraga, the strongest

173
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,600
shikigami of the technique.

174
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,920
It adapts to whatever hits it, and the

175
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:16,280
wheel on its back turns as it learns.

176
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,380
And the ritual to summon it doesn't end

177
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:22,160
until either its target is dead, or it's

178
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:22,480
tamed.

179
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,780
In the story, the only one who ever

180
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:27,000
tamed it was Sukuna.

181
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,480
You close your eyes.

182
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,300
The wheel stops turning.

183
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,080
You don't tell anyone.

184
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:35,500
Lesson ten: there's one door in your shadow

185
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,160
you can't walk back through.

186
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:41,520
On day twenty-five, a child goes missing at

187
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,120
the edge of the city, and the search

188
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,160
party is walking in lines with torches.

189
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,940
You stand at the treeline with your hand

190
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,100
over your shadow.

191
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,620
The dogs take the scent from the child's

192
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,740
coat, and they go.

193
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,920
White and black, low through the trees, silent.

194
00:06:57,620 --> 00:07:00,680
They find her in forty minutes, asleep under

195
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,920
a fallen trunk, with a muddy shoe in

196
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,460
her arms.

197
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:05,080
Nobody asks how.

198
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,040
They're too busy hugging her.

199
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,480
Lesson eleven: sometimes the point isn't what you

200
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,040
can do.

201
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,980
It's what you do with it.

202
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:17,140
By day thirty you can feel exactly how

203
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,380
much each of them costs.

204
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,000
The dogs are cheap.

205
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,620
The toad is cheap.

206
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,500
The elephant leaves you in bed for a

207
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:24,840
day.

208
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,240
You're treating your own shadow like a bank

209
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:30,180
account, and you're afraid to check the balance.

210
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,420
Lesson twelve: you're never out of shadows.

211
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,780
You're only ever out of you.

212
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:39,980
On day forty, at night, a floor of

213
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:42,600
the car park near your flat collapses with

214
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,400
eleven people underneath it.

215
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,360
You run.

216
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,580
You're the only one who can do anything.

217
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:50,360
There's one thing in your shadow that could

218
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:52,060
lift the slab with one hand.

219
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,180
You can feel it turning.

220
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,260
You stand at the edge of the rubble

221
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:59,640
with your hand over your shadow, and you

222
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,140
take it away.

223
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:02,220
So you do the other thing.

224
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:05,380
You spread your shadow across the floor, the

225
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:07,920
way you practised on the pitch, over whatever's

226
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,480
already there.

227
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,120
It doesn't need to be perfect.

228
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,160
It only needs to be big enough.

229
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,160
The dogs find them by smell, under the

230
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:15,520
concrete.

231
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:18,440
The toad pulls them out, one by one,

232
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,360
with its tongue.

233
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,640
The serpent slides under the beams.

234
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:24,540
The elephant stands up under the slab and

235
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:27,040
holds it, and your legs shake the whole

236
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:27,360
time.

237
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,340
Eleven people come out.

238
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,380
Nobody asks what you are.

239
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:34,380
The next morning you can't get out of

240
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:34,560
bed.

241
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,720
Now you know what it really is.

242
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,780
Not a gift.

243
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,780
A door in the floor,

244
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:42,460
and you're the only one who decides what

245
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,340
comes through.

246
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:47,180
Lesson thirteen: the strongest thing in your shadow

247
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,740
is the one you didn't open.

248
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,940
The next night at three fifteen, you lift

249
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,300
your arm, and your shadow doesn't move.

250
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:56,560
You wait.

251
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,620
Something stirs under it, and it sits.

252
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:01,320
It's the white dog.

253
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,700
So if you woke up tomorrow with Megumi's

254
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:07,060
Ten Shadows, which one would you call first?

255
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:09,980
And would you ever open the one that

256
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:11,800
can only be stopped by killing you?

257
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:12,980
Tell me in the comments.
